  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">North Africa migration and development (NAMAD) &#x2013; phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The North Africa Migration and Development (NAMAD) project aims to enhance skills and labour market integration for migrant and host communities, and to strengthen protection support for vulnerable migrants, in Algeria, Egypt and Tunisia. Based on the needs in each country context, IOM&#x2019;s targeted interventions will address specific barriers and gaps by providing a range of skills development and training, and providing tailored humanitarian and protection support for migrants in vulnerable situations. This will include provision of shelter, case management, multi-purpose cash assistance and non-food items to meet basic needs, medical support, mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) and legal counselling.</narrative>
  </description>
